Package: dictate
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Javier Santacruz <javier.santacruz.lc@gmail.com>
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), python3-gi, gir1.2-ibus-1.0, ibus, wl-clipboard, pipewire-bin, libnotify-bin, libglib2.0-bin, gsettings-desktop-schemas, gnome-settings-daemon-common
Recommends: dictate-indicator, ydotool (>= 1.0), sound-theme-freedesktop
Suggests: dictate-whisper, tmux, dictate-uinput
Homepage: https://github.com/jvrsantacruz/dictate
Description: dictation into the focused input on GNOME on Wayland
 Press a shortcut, speak, press it again: the speech is transcribed by a
 whisper server and the text is inserted into the input that had focus at
 the first press. An IBus engine inserts it and tells whether focus moved;
 when it did, the text goes to the clipboard instead.
 .
 Run `dictate setup` once per user to set the shortcuts, the input source
 and the config, and again after an upgrade, so IBus runs the new engine.
 The transcriber is not part of this package: dictate-whisper is a local one,
 or point dictate at any whisper server.
 .
 The paste and type methods need write access to /dev/uinput, which the
 dictate-uinput package grants to the user at the seat. It is only suggested:
 the grant is the admin's choice to make.
